# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for OBX_SAN=thread (rt.py).
# Microsoft's ODBC driver is closed source and not built with TSan, so the
# synchronization inside it is invisible: two connections opened at once on
# two helper threads report races on the driver's own heap blocks, under its
# own mutexes, with no obx frame below the driver's. This hides any report
# whose stack passes through the driver, including one on memory obx passed
# to it; those buffers are borrowed by the parked task for the whole call
# (SPEC 12), which the checked tests cover.
race:libmsodbcsql
